  "Four pairs of bars: for small things the guess towers over the truth, for the largest the truth runs well past the guess": "四組の棒。小さいものでは推定が実際をはるかに上回り、最大のものでは実際が推定をはるかに上回る",
  "Two maps side by side: the familiar-looking one draws the far north far too large, the stranger-looking one draws both bands in true proportion and is the accurate one": "並んだ二枚の地図。見慣れた方は極北を大きく描きすぎ、見慣れない方は二つの帯を正しい比率で描いていて、そちらが正確",
  "Two bars of equal length against the same target line, one with a wide band of finishers crowded against the line and one with a narrow band": "同じ目標線に対して同じ長さの二本の棒。一方は線の直前に密集した幅広の帯、もう一方は細い帯",
